    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d398">

                <pb facs="0517" n="432" sameAs="frus:frus1919v02/pg432"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/3169a: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to the Minister in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Reinsch</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-07-14T19:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">July 14, 1919,
                                7 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>Department informed July 11<anchor n="39" xml:id="d398-f1"/> by Japanese Embassy
                    that careful instructions had been cabled to Japanese Minister to consult you
                    frankly and fully and to co-operate with you in an effort to straighten out the
                    difficulty at Tientsin.</p>
                <p>You will please be guided by Department’s recent cable in the same matter.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Polk</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
